@*
===========================================================
ORANGE TENDER MANAGEMENT SYSTEM
PAGE: Forward Bids to Evaluation Committee

DEVELOPER OWNER: Saja
MODULE: Sourcing Officer / Bid Management
TRELLO TASK: Forward Bids to Evaluation Committee
TRELLO URL: Not provided — add from the Trello board

PURPOSE:
Check the minimum-offer rule for the round and forward it to
the Evaluation Committee.

BUSINESS ACCESS:
Sourcing Officer

ROUTE: /SourcingOfficer/Bids/ForwardToCommittee/{id?}

FUTURE IMPLEMENTATION:
- Count DISTINCT suppliers with a Submitted bid in this
  TenderRound only.
- Apply the 3-offer rule (or the 2-offer exception) in a
  tested service.
- Require 4 assigned Evaluation Committee members and a
  submitted OfficerComparison report.
- POST: update statuses, create the CommitteeRound, notify
  members, audit.

DEPENDENCIES:
TenderRounds, TenderInvitations, Bids, CommitteeMembers,
CommitteeRounds, TenderReports, Notifications.

STATUS:
UI SCAFFOLD ONLY — BUSINESS LOGIC NOT IMPLEMENTED.

IMPORTANT:
Do not implement the counting or forwarding in the view;
keep it in a service with tests.
===========================================================
*@
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Forward Bids to Evaluation Committee";
    ViewData["WorkspaceSection"] = "Received Bids";
    ViewData["Description"] = "Send the round’s offers and the comparison report to the four-member Evaluation Committee.";
}
<partial name="_PageHeader" />
<partial name="_ScaffoldNotice" />

<section class="ws-panel pg-panel">
    <h2>Round summary</h2>
    <dl class="pg-dl">
        <div><dt>Tender</dt><dd>—</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Round number</dt><dd>—</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Submitted offers from distinct suppliers</dt><dd>—</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Minimum required for this round</dt><dd>—</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Comparison report version</dt><dd>—</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Evaluation Committee members assigned</dt><dd>—</dd></div>
    </dl>
</section>

<aside class="pg-note"><strong>Minimum-offer rule</strong><p>Normally at least 3 submitted offers from 3 different suppliers are required; invitations do not count. After three unsuccessful tendering attempts, the approved exception allows proceeding with 2 offers. The exact attempt-counting convention is finalized in business logic.</p></aside>

<partial name="_ConfirmAction" model='new ConfirmActionModel("Forward to Evaluation Committee", "Send this round to the Evaluation Committee.", "Sets the round to SentToEvaluation, creates an Evaluation CommitteeRound and attaches the Officer’s comparison report.", false, false)' />
